    female|a||The widest bar — here the QALY gain — is the parameter whose resolution could most change the answer.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7360
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical'
    female|a||Run the same exercise on statins in primary prevention and no single bar crosses zero at all — a tornado that stays on one side of the line is itself the finding.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 11560
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical'
    'female|a||Now the structural weakness: every bar moves its parameter alone, with all the others frozen at base case.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7600
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:197i86n'
    female|a||Real discounts arrive tied to a duration cap and a stopping rule — move price and years together and the true swing is wider than either bar shows.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10200
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:1g57ppu'
    female|a||And the ends of a bar are ranges an analyst chose, not outcomes with any likelihood attached.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6400
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:1pndzaq'
    female|a||What can a tornado diagram NOT tell you?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 3080
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:byv3g4'
    female|a||It shows how far the result can move, never how probable that move is — the bars carry no probabilities.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7520
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical'
    female|a|grave|A tornado names the assumptions a decision hangs on, and by staying silent about probability, shows exactly why one-way analysis can never be the last word.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 15760
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical'
    'female|a|brisk|Next: let every parameter move at once, a thousand times over.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 4400
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:1d4mt9s'
    'female|a||The recipe is a sweep: fix a threshold lambda, and count how many of the thousand draws have a positive net monetary benefit — lambda times delta E, minus delta C.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12120
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:8oq8tk'
    female|a||That share is one height on the curve for nusinersen; sweep lambda from left to right and the shares join up into this line. Read the axis in thousands of kroner per QALY.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 12360
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:joyj04'
    'female|a||The dashed line marks a half: above it, the drug has the higher net benefit in more runs than it loses.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7080
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:mq7uh'
    'female|a||At 275,000 kroner per QALY — the ordinary end of the Norwegian range — this illustrative curve sits on the floor: almost no draw makes the drug the better buy.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11200
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:107jtob'
    female|a||Push lambda up to 825,000, the top of the severity-adjusted range, and the curve has climbed to roughly seven runs in ten.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8480
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:vxhguy'
    'female|a||Current care is the exact mirror image: at every lambda one option has the higher net benefit, so the two probabilities always sum to one.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9480
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:vqtquk'
    'female|a||And read the shape: flat across most of the axis, turning inside one narrow band — everywhere outside that band, the answer is not close.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9840
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:1fi802r'
    'female|a||The device dates from the mid-1990s, invented to dodge a genuine statistical problem: the ICER is a ratio, and when delta E can sit near zero, its confidence interval stops behaving.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12640
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:1ob0dsr'
    female|a||Now the claim itself — probability 0.7 cost-effective — and what it does not say.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6840
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:1mavm1g'
    'female|a|grave|It is not a clinical probability: it does not say seven in ten children will benefit. The effect size sits inside the model as one uncertain parameter, already averaged over patients.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 17000
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:9e3luw'
    'female|a||Nor is it a claim about whether the drug works: a treatment with a rock-solid, well-measured benefit can still read 0.3, purely because its price outruns lambda.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10800
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:1i7ywxj'
    female|a||What the 0.7 counts is our ignorance about the inputs — utilities, transition probabilities, price, discounting — pushed through the model and tallied at one threshold.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 11280
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:16lz1qv'
    female|a||A quick check on the claim. The curve reads about 0.7 at lambda = 825,000 kr per QALY. What does that mean?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9840
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:188qmr9'
    'female|a||It is a statement about parameter uncertainty: in seven runs out of ten, lambda times delta E exceeded delta C.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10040
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical'
    female|a||The manufacturer halves the price. What happens to nusinersen's curve?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5480
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical'
    female|a||A lower delta C raises net benefit at every lambda, so the whole curve shifts left.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5960
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical'
    'female|a||So the acceptability curve answers one question only: at each price we are willing to pay for a year of health, how confident is the model — not whether the drug works.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11600
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical'
    female|a||Back to the nusinersen model in illustrative numbers — net monetary benefit per patient — and the widest bar is how long the treatment effect is assumed to last.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 11880
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:6a125w'
    female|a||Time horizon, price, the four percent discount rate and averted care costs follow, each swing narrower than the one above it.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9200
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:3i42a6'
    female|a||Only that top bar reaches far enough to carry the result across into positive net benefit; the bottom two barely move it at all.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8400
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:11rd071'
    female|a||A quick check before we synthesise. What does the widest bar of a tornado diagram tell you?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6280
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:h2ojt1'
    female|a||The widest bar marks the parameter the result is most sensitive to — nothing about how likely its values are.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7600
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical'
    female|a||So set the whole toolkit down in one table, and read it column by column.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5400
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical'
    'female|a||Best case and worst case: two stories with nothing in between, and no claim at all about how likely either one is.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8240
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:u6q3uc'
    female|a||Struck out, because it is the only display here that answers no question a decision maker actually asked.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6720
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:1g927cb'
    female|a||The tornado ranks where to look first — but it moves inputs one at a time, and attaches no probability to any of them.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8600
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:xgmozb'
    female|a||The cloud of a thousand draws shows how far ΔC and ΔE can land together — but only for the inputs we chose to give a distribution.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8920
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:yy5en0'
    'female|a||And the acceptability curve compresses that cloud into one number per threshold: the share of draws in which the new technology wins.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8920
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:v871rr'
    'female|a||One more. A CEAC reads 0.7 at the severity-weighted λ. That means:':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7400
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:1hjncne'
    'female|a||It is a property of the simulation: in seven draws out of ten, net benefit at that threshold is positive.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7560
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical'
    'female|a||The real limit sits in that last cell: every one of those draws came from the same structure, the same states, the same extrapolation.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10080
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical'
    female|a||All four displays vary the numbers inside the model. Not one of them varies the model.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6080
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:13lymor'
    female|a|grave|For nusinersen that is the decisive gap — a trial measured in months, projected across a childhood, and no distribution on the parameters can widen that assumption.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 15960
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:13irnhz'
    'female|a||So: scenarios say nothing, the tornado says where to look, the cloud says how wide the answer is, the curve says how often it clears the threshold — and showing what you don''t know still leaves what you never modelled.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 14560
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical #ctx:10mth51'
    female|a||Best case against worst case is scenario theatre; here is the disciplined version of that instinct — one that tells a committee which assumption the whole decision is hanging on.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 12120
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical'
    female|a||A thousand draws scattered across the plane is a cloud no committee can read — so squeeze it into one line that a decision maker can.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9880
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical'
    'female|a||Tornado, cloud and curve: line up every display this lecture built and ask what each one honestly answers.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8560
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical'
    female|a||Equal likelihood is something readers assume; the table itself carries no probabilities at all.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6400
      voice: 'gemini:Charon | a clear, warm university lecturer: measured, engaged, never theatrical'
    female|a||The threshold and the discount rate are the same in every cell; what changes is that this corner stacks two extremes.:
